{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671601-a-question-on-true-fae","id":671601,"title":"A Question on True Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T19:32:35-07:00","id":671601,"title":"A Question on True Fae","content":"So, I've a question about True Fae in the World of Darkness. I know they're generally more plot-device than actual character if they appear at all in a Changeling chronicle, but I was wondering if any of the splats list any form of unique powers, arts or traits for them.<br /> <br /> Also, if a PC Changeling's aim was to cease being a Changeling and return to their existence prior to the Changeling Way, how would they go about this? I presume obviously that there are no rules, and in strictest meta it is probably impossible, but let's presume that it is. Would it be a gradual change, a sudden change? What would change about the Changeling in terms of personality and mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:51:00-07:00","id":671706,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think a Changeling CAN turn into a True Fae, but only by standing just outside of the Arcadian Gates for decades and decades. I think it's in Dreams and Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T03:47:27-07:00","id":671780,"title":"","content":"Well, as interesting as that is, I think in this particular instance it's not going to end up hugely relevant, as the chronicle isn't going to allow for a few decades standing outside the Gates of Arcadia. Heck even finding them in the first place would seem to me like the ending of a Campaign of Chronicles.<br /> <br /> What kind of thematic/homebrew style alternatives would we suggest?<br /> <br /> I'm still very curious to hear either if WW gave any guidelines for the powers of True Fae, or whether there are any particularly good fan splats for, or even what people's suggestions and thoughts as to their powers should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:21:24-07:00","id":671959,"title":"","content":"You can use Dark Ages Fae to represent True Fae, that's pretty much what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:01:31-07:00","id":672047,"title":"","content":"In that case would &quot;True Fae&quot; equal &quot;Firstborn&quot;? And &quot;Changeling&quot; (modern) = &quot;Changeling&quot; (DA) with the two distinguished by the body-hopping of the Changeling Way for the former?<br /> <br /> There isn't a current system for Changelings (DA) becoming Firstborn. (Man, so many Firstborn would have seen that as the WORST THING EVER). A little chimerical sprite had more chance of becoming a Firstborn than anything ever born human. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, I guess one could try to shed the Changeling Way, but then you'd end up with a DA Changeling (after all, no matter what's going on with the soul, the &quot;born human&quot; part still matters). Which might be cool for what it would be worth. It might be fun trying out the DA Fae powers over the mess in CtD, but you'd need to make this life MATTER as it would be the very last one you're going to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:02:13-07:00","id":672058,"title":"","content":"Seconding Coridan. DA: Fae is all about the fae in the time leading up to the Shattering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:24:59-07:00","id":672080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671601-a-question-on-true-fae#post671601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've a question about True Fae in the World of Darkness. I know they're generally more plot-device than actual character if they appear at all in a Changeling chronicle, but I was wondering if any of the splats list any form of unique powers, arts or traits for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Introduced in <b>Nobles: the Shining Host</b>, the Lost Ones are still True Fae. As the Shattering swept the world, some (individual) fae barricaded themselves in freeholds, walling themselves off from mundane reality (and Banality). It worked . . . but at a price. Every Lost One went completely mad (granted some more benignly than others), and can no longer leave their refuges.<br /> <br /> As for powers . . . they're pretty godlike. I don't remember if we got stats for them or not, but we did see one in action (in the third part of the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> chronicle). There, a Lost One raised an island from the bottom of the sea, with little more than a wave of his hands. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if a PC Changeling's aim was to cease being a Changeling and return to their existence prior to the Changeling Way, how would they go about this? I presume obviously that there are no rules, and in strictest meta it is probably impossible, but let's presume that it is. . . </div> </div> </div>That was actually the prize for successfully completing the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> chronicle. Created at/by the fall of the Court of All Kings (and a selkie queen's curse), the four gems were scattered across the face of the Earth in the wake of the Shattering. Each had lesser abilities, but - if brought together at Silver's Gate - had a unique <i>major</i> power:<ul><li>The sapphire can lead you (safely) to anything - even fabled Arcadia</li> <li>The emerald can open any lock - even the ones that seal the gates of Arcadia</li> <li>The ruby undoes the Changeling Way, turning a changeling back into a true fae</li> <li>The black (Obsidian?) gem permanently cleanses them of Banality</li> </ul>Of course, the caveat is that completing that campaign takes four characters permanently out of play . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:53:16-07:00","id":673276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671601-a-question-on-true-fae?p=672080#post672080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Introduced in <b>Nobles: the Shining Host</b>, the Lost Ones are still True Fae. As the Shattering swept the world, some (individual) fae barricaded themselves in freeholds, walling themselves off from mundane reality (and Banality). It worked . . . but at a price. Every Lost One went completely mad (granted some more benignly than others), and can no longer leave their refuges.<br /> <br /> As for powers . . . they're pretty godlike. I don't remember if we got stats for them or not, but we did see one in action (in the third part of the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> chronicle). There, a Lost One raised an island from the bottom of the sea, with little more than a wave of his hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> That was actually the prize for successfully completing the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> chronicle. Created at/by the fall of the Court of All Kings (and a selkie queen's curse), the four gems were scattered across the face of the Earth in the wake of the Shattering. Each had lesser abilities, but - if brought together at Silver's Gate - had a unique <i>major</i> power:<ul><li>The sapphire can lead you (safely) to anything - even fabled Arcadia</li> <li>The emerald can open any lock - even the ones that seal the gates of Arcadia</li> <li>The ruby undoes the Changeling Way, turning a changeling back into a true fae</li> <li>The black (Obsidian?) gem permanently cleanses them of Banality</li> </ul>Of course, the caveat is that completing that campaign takes four characters permanently out of play . . .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This answer is particularly interesting. I'd not read the Immortal Eyes chronicle before you'd mentioned it. Some of the consequences of that campaign set an interesting precedent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just to clarify earlier points, when I mean True Fae, I do generally mean Firstborn or their horrific equivalents. Dark Ages: Fae, whilst a very interesting line, do not get me wrong, are still fairly thematically the same as Changelings, in that they aren't really the true denizens of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> As for how important being born human is, I think that's particularly up in the air. I'm inclined to think it's only 'really' a hindrance because of the limitations of mortality and the human shell. Reversing the Changeling Way and eschewing a the limitations of mortality seems to me a particularly interesting development process. I agree that Dark Ages: Fae lay somewhere between True Fae and Changelings on the spectrum. What's particularly interesting for me I think is the number of unexpected consequences that could be generated by a Changeling essentially trying to free his/her soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:21:35-07:00","id":676544,"title":"","content":"Was there even a Dreaming before the Sundering? Maybe that's what &quot;Sundering&quot; means. The Dreaming was woven into the world until it wasn't anymore. Reading DA:Fae, the places where the fae live seems awfully like what the Dreaming should be, just plunked down on a mundane map.<br /> <br /> In which case the Firstborn ARE the True Fae, or, at least the True Fae before they were one step even more removed from the mortal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T01:17:14-07:00","id":680752,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming wasn't separate from the real world until the Sundering, IIRC. They flowed together. I find it best to think of the contemporary Dreaming as the last refuge of the mythic and wonderful that used to exist in the mortal world and which can now only thrive on the power of dreams and imagination because reality itself can't sustain that magic any more.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn pretty much are True Fae. Perhaps they were stronger at the dawn of time, but they're otherwise the same basic premise. They may not choose to adopt a mortal form ever, and you might want to make Unleashing easier, but that's it, I reckon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:00:13-07:00","id":683814,"title":"","content":"Aren't the Dark Kin technically True Fae? I mean the Denizens never became Changelings and only recently arrived from the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}